{:paths ["src"]

 ;; No dependencies at all, and that is the point.
 ;;
 ;; raylib and SDL2 are STATIC ARCHIVES linked into the executable by
 ;; tools/ios/build.sh, not shared libraries loaded at run time -- `jolt build
 ;; --target` emits the whole binary and Chez owns main, so there is no host
 ;; process to dlopen anything and every defcfn resolves against the process
 ;; image at first call. A :jolt/native entry naming libraylib.dylib (which is
 ;; what both published raylib bindings declare) would be actively wrong here:
 ;; jolt loads a dependency's natives transitively, before any namespace, and
 ;; hard-fails when one is missing. There is no .dylib in an .ipa.
 ;;
 ;; The raylib surface this project calls -- some thirty-five functions -- is
 ;; declared inline in raylib.host, mirroring what the demo did. Taking
 ;; jlt-commons/raylib-jlt as a real dependency would mean dealing with its own
 ;; :jolt/native declaration; jolt's `:process true` is the door if the other
 ;; four hundred functions are ever wanted.
 :deps {}
 :jolt/native []

 ;; ffi/write took (p t offset v) before 0.8.0 and (p t v offset) after, and the
 ;; two cannot be told apart at runtime -- both arguments are integers, so an
 ;; older jolt would write the wrong byte to the wrong place in silence rather
 ;; than refuse. Every struct here goes through ffi/layout + write-field, which
 ;; is stable across both, and this floor is belt and braces.
 :jolt/min-version "0.8.0"

 :aliases
 {:test {:extra-paths ["test"]
         :main-opts ["-m" "raylib.test-runner"]}}

 :tasks
 {;; the two static archives, per SDK. Slow the first time, cached after.
  deps    "sh tools/ios/deps.sh"
  ;; cross-compile NS into RaylibIOS.app. NS=raylib.gallery TARGET=device jolt build-app
  build-app "sh tools/ios/build.sh"
  ;; sign, install and launch on the phone. UDID=<hardware udid> jolt deploy
  deploy  "sh tools/ios/deploy.sh"
  ;; the pure namespaces, on the host: no raylib, no SDL, no device
  test    "jolt -M:test"
  ;; the gallery plus an nREPL, for driving a running app from an editor.
  ;; Dev only: App Store rule 2.5.2 bans executing downloaded code, and a
  ;; shipped build carries no listener.
  live    "sh tools/ios/live.sh"
  ;; jolt.nrepl binds loopback only, so reach it by forwarding the phone's
  ;; 7888 to this machine's 7889 over USB. Needs the cable: iproxy speaks
  ;; usbmuxd, which a Wi-Fi-only pairing does not answer.
  ;; Refuses to bind beside a process that already holds the local port,
  ;; because forwarding onto one sends evals to THAT process and its answers
  ;; look entirely plausible. LOCAL_PORT and DEVICE_PORT override.
  proxy   "sh tools/ios/proxy.sh"
  ;; what deploy would talk to. devicectl's cached list lies about state, so
  ;; this asks each device for its tunnelState instead of trusting the summary.
  devices "sh tools/ios/devices.sh"}}
